    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #8692.\n\nIn `DeepSpeedZeroOptimizer_Stage3`, `__avg_scatter_contiguous_grads` (`stage3.py:1877`) and `allreduce_bucket` (`stage3.py:2278`) both divide the gradient averaging world size by `float(self.sequence_parallel_size)`, matching ZeRO-0 (`engine.py:3884`) and ZeRO-1/2 (`stage_1_and_2.py:1505, 1687, 2379`).\n\nHowever, `__avg_scatter_grads` (`stage3.py:1936-1940`) delegates to `reduce_scatter_coalesced` (which divides by `partition_world_size`) and only rescales when `averaging_world_size != partition_world_size` without accounting for `self.sequence_parallel_size`:\n\n```python\npartition_world_size = dist.get_world_size(group=process_group)\naveraging_world_size = self._gradient_averaging_world_size(\n    params_to_reduce, partition_world_size) / float(self.sequence_parallel_size)\nif averaging_world_size != partition_world_size:\n    scale = partition_world_size / float(averaging_world_size)\n    grad_partitions_for_rank = [g.mul(scale) for g in grad_partitions_for_rank]\n```\n\nWithout this division by `float(self.sequence_parallel_size)`:\n1. Under `sequence_parallel_size > 1`, ZeRO-3 with `reduce_scatter=True` or `contiguous_gradients=False` produces gradients smaller by a factor of `sequence_parallel_size` than `reduce_scatter=False, contiguous_gradients=True` or ZeRO-1/2.\n2. Even within a single ZeRO-3 model using `reduce_scatter=False, contiguous_gradients=True`, parameters whose size exceeds `reduce_bucket_size` fall back to `__avg_scatter_grads` (`stage3.py:1686`), while smaller parameters use `__avg_scatter_contiguous_grads` (`stage3.py:1683`), causing different layers of the same model to receive gradients scaled by `1 / sp_size` vs `1.0` in the same backward step.\n\n## Non-duplication Check\n\n- Checked #8692 (`closed_by_pull_requests: 0`) and searched open/closed PRs touching `stage3.py`, `__avg_scatter_grads`, and `sequence_parallel_size`.\n- Related PRs do not touch this path:\n  - #8668 fixes `gradient_predivide_factor == partition_world_size` post-scaling in `stage3.py`.\n  - #8687 fixes `gradient_predivide_factor` post-scaling in `stage_1_and_2.py`.\n  - #8457 and #8811 only touch `compile/` AutoSP passes and `groups.py`.\n\n## Validation & Test Results\n\nAdded `TestZero3SequenceParallelGradientScale` in `tests/unit/v1/zero/test_zero.py` covering all four ZeRO-3 reduction configurations under `sequence_parallel_size=2` (`(reduce_scatter=False, contiguous_gradients=True, reduce_bucket_size=500)`, `(False, False, 500)`, `(True, True, 500)`, and mixed-bucket `(False, True, 16)` where `small` takes `__avg_scatter_contiguous_grads` and `large` takes `__avg_scatter_grads`).\n\n### Commands Run\n\n1. **New regression test (`TestZero3SequenceParallelGradientScale`)**:\n   ```bash\n   PYTHONPATH=.:\"$PWD/tests\" DS_ACCELERATOR=cpu LOCAL_SIZE=2 pytest tests/unit/v1/zero/test_zero.py -k \"TestZero3SequenceParallelGradientScale\" -v\n   ```\n   - **Before fix**: 3 failed (`test[False-False-500]`, `test[True-True-500]`, `test[False-True-16]`), 1 passed (`test[False-True-500]`).\n   - **After fix**: `4 passed in 23.18s`.\n\n2. **Existing ZeRO gradient reduction tests (`TestGradientAllreduceOp`)**:\n   ```bash\n   PYTHONPATH=.:\"$PWD/tests\" DS_ACCELERATOR=cpu LOCAL_SIZE=2 pytest tests/unit/v1/zero/test_zero.py -k \"TestGradientAllreduceOp and not Training\" -v\n   ```\n   - **Result**: `18 passed in 90.64s`.\n\n### Compatibility Matrix\n\n| Feature / Path | Validated Locally | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ZeRO-3 (`reduce_scatter=False, contiguous_gradients=True`) | Yes (2-rank CPU/Gloo) | Matches `1.0` scale |\n| ZeRO-3 (`reduce_scatter=False, contiguous_gradients=False`) | Yes (2-rank CPU/Gloo) | Fixed from `1/sp` to `1.0` |\n| ZeRO-3 (`reduce_scatter=True, contiguous_gradients=True`) | Yes (2-rank CPU/Gloo) | Fixed from `1/sp` to `1.0` |\n| ZeRO-3 mixed bucket (`param.ds_numel > reduce_bucket_size`) | Yes (2-rank CPU/Gloo) | Both small and large params get `1.0` scale |\n| ZeRO-0 / ZeRO-1 / ZeRO-2 | Yes (2-rank CPU/Gloo) | Unchanged (`18 passed`) |\n| Multi-node `all_to_all_quant_reduce` | Not run locally (single-node host) | Uses same post-reduction `averaging_world_size` rescale |\n\n### Environment (`ds_report`)\n\n- OS: Linux aarch64 (Debian 13)\n- Python: 3.13.5, PyTorch: 2.14.1+cpu (`DS_ACCELERATOR=cpu`, Gloo backend, 2 processes)\n\n## AI Assistance Disclosure\n\nAI assistance (GitHub Copilot) was used to help draft the regression test and PR description; all root-cause analysis and test executions were run and verified locally.\n\n### Credits & Acknowledgments\n- Full credit to **@alanhuangyoo** for reporting #8692, diagnosing the exact gradient-scaling discrepancy between `__avg_scatter_grads` and `__avg_scatter_contiguous_grads` / `allreduce_bucket` under sequence parallelism (including the mixed-bucket single-model case), and providing the 2-rank reproduction scripts; and to **@Eliaaazzz** for citing #4530 and `_reduce_non_expert_gradients` confirming the DP-world averaging convention.\n- If @alanhuangyoo would like to submit their own PR as offered in #8692, we are more than happy to yield/close this PR in favor of theirs or add `Co-authored-by:`.\n",
